# 👥 Linux User and Permission Management

## 📌 Objective

The purpose of this lab is to learn how to manage users, groups and file permissions on an Ubuntu Linux system.

User and permission management is one of the core responsibilities of a Linux system administrator. Proper configuration ensures that users can access only the resources required for their work while protecting the operating system from unauthorized modifications.

At the end of this lab, multiple user accounts will be created, organized into groups, granted appropriate permissions and tested in a realistic administration scenario.

