# 👤 Creating User Accounts

Three user accounts were created to represent employees of the company.

| Username | Role |
|----------|------|
| alice | System Administrator |
| bob | System Administrator |
| charlie | Software Developer |

Each account was created with its own home directory and Bash as the default login shell.

```bash
sudo useradd -m -s /bin/bash alice
sudo useradd -m -s /bin/bash bob
sudo useradd -m -s /bin/bash charlie
```

Passwords were then assigned to each account.

```bash
sudo passwd alice
sudo passwd bob
sudo passwd charlie
```

The newly created users were verified using:

```bash
cat /etc/passwd | grep -E "alice|bob|charlie"
```

and

```bash
id alice
id bob
id charlie
```

The output confirmed that each user account had been successfully created with its own user ID (UID), primary group and home directory.

