# 👥 Assigning Users to Security Groups

After creating the user accounts, each employee was assigned to the appropriate security group.

The two system administrators were added to the **sysadmins** group.

The developer was added to the **developers** group.

```bash
sudo usermod -aG sysadmins alice
sudo usermod -aG sysadmins bob
sudo usermod -aG developers charlie
```

The configuration was verified using:

```bash
id alice
id bob
id charlie
```

The output confirmed that:

- Alice belongs to the **sysadmins** group.
- Bob belongs to the **sysadmins** group.
- Charlie belongs to the **developers** group.

This group-based organization simplifies permission management and follows standard Linux administration practices.

![Group membership verification](../../screenshots/lab-05/03-group-membership.png)
