# 📁 Creating the Company Directory Structure

To simulate a real company environment, two shared directories were created under **/opt/company**.

The following commands were executed:

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /opt/company/admins
sudo mkdir -p /opt/company/projects
```

The resulting directory structure was verified using:

```bash
tree /opt/company
```

The output confirmed the following hierarchy:

```text
/opt/company
├── admins
└── projects
```

The **admins** directory will be shared by the system administrators, while the **projects** directory will be used by the development team.

![Company directory structure](../../screenshots/lab-05/04-directory-structure.png)

