# 👑 Configuring Directory Ownership

Once the directory structure had been created, ownership was configured to associate each directory with its corresponding security group.

The following commands were executed:

```bash
sudo chown root:sysadmins /opt/company/admins
sudo chown root:developers /opt/company/projects
```

The ownership was verified using:

```bash
ls -ld /opt/company/admins
ls -ld /opt/company/projects
```

The output confirmed that:

- the **admins** directory belongs to the **sysadmins** group;
- the **projects** directory belongs to the **developers** group.

Using **root** as the owner while assigning the appropriate group allows administrators to centrally manage access through Linux group permissions.

![Directory ownership](../../screenshots/lab-05/05-directory-ownership.png)

