# 🔐 Configuring Directory Permissions

After assigning ownership, directory permissions were configured to allow collaboration within each team.

The following commands were executed:

```bash
sudo chmod 2775 /opt/company/admins
sudo chmod 2775 /opt/company/projects
```

The permissions were verified using:

```bash
ls -ld /opt/company/admins
ls -ld /opt/company/projects
```

The output displayed permissions similar to:

```text
drwxrwsr-x
```

The permission value **2775** has the following meaning:

- **2** enables the **Set Group ID (SGID)** bit;
- **7** grants the owner read, write and execute permissions;
- **7** grants the group read, write and execute permissions;
- **5** grants read and execute permissions to other users.

This configuration allows members of each group to collaborate while preventing unauthorized modifications by users outside the group.

![Directory permissions](../../screenshots/lab-05/06-directory-permissions.png)

