# 📝 Conclusion

This lab demonstrated the implementation of user and permission management on an Ubuntu Linux server.

A realistic company scenario was used to create user accounts, organize users into security groups and configure access to shared resources.

Directory ownership and permissions were configured following Linux administration best practices, including the use of the **Set Group ID (SGID)** bit to ensure consistent group ownership within shared directories.

Administrative privileges were delegated only to authorized users through the **sudo** group, while standard users remained restricted from performing privileged operations.

The completed configuration provides a secure and maintainable access control model based on Linux users, groups and file permissions, illustrating essential skills required for Linux system administration.
